  Will Users Buy It? Honest Answer
  
  The free tier gives away the most valuable thing — anomaly detection. A user can upload their payslip, see "Missing TPTA this month" or "DSOP
  contribution below 6%", and fix the issue — all for free. The premium gate (AiInsightsBottomSheet) only adds a narrative paragraph around what the free
  cards already show.

  That's the real monetization problem, not the AI architecture.

  The target cohort (Indian Army PCDA(O) officers) will pay for:
  1. Something that recovers their money — anomaly detection already does this (free)
  2. Something that protects their privacy — offline is compelling here
  3. Something that takes action for them — representation letters that actually get sent

  Right now premium = "better story around findings you already have." That's weak.

  ---
  My Recommendation: Defer Gemma, Fix the App
  
  Skip Gemma entirely for the next 3 months. Not because it's a bad idea — it's the right long-term call — but because you have higher-ROI work sitting
  untouched.

  What to build instead (prioritised):

  Sprint 1 — Remove blockers
  - Fix iOS parser freeze (replace per-character loop with bounds indexing)
  - Replace println() with structured logging
  - Add parser error recovery (silent failures are invisible to users)

  Sprint 2 — Make premium worth buying
  - Representation letter: add WhatsApp/email share (1 day of work, huge value for the cohort)
  - DSOP Simulator: make the slider interactive ("what if I increase contribution by 2%?")
  - Retroactive audit: run all 9 auditors across all uploaded months and surface a "historical anomaly" list (the data is already in LedgerRecordEntity —
  you're just not showing it)

  Sprint 3 — Add features that use existing data
  - YoY salary comparison chart (uses LedgerRecordEntity which is already populated but never displayed)
  - Export financial summary as PDF for tax filing season (high value, medium effort)
  - Tax regime toggle (old vs new) in WealthOptimizationEngine — currently hardcoded to old regime

  Then revisit Gemma / Foundation Models once the above is done and you have users paying for premium.

